{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0164ZsHhm1nfu1rU3K1UvjoT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## 2026-08-31 — WI-540: the adjudicator session-retention layer, shipped inert at dial 0\n2\t\n3\tPlan §5 step 3 of the adjudicator session-retention plan\n4\t(`docs/plans/2026-08-29-adjudicator-session-retention-plan.md`). The layer that\n5\tturns WI-535's telemetry into an opt-in retained session: a session store, a\n6\tper-family resume-argv adapter, occupancy readers, the drain/reset rule and the\n7\tkeep-warm tick — all guarded behind `[adjudicator] context_reset_pct`, shipped\n8\tat `0` (inert: today's one-shot behaviour byte-for-byte). Turning the dial on\n9\tand verifying it on-box is WI-541 (plan §5 step 4).\n10\t\n11\tOwner rulings honoured (OI-69, `docs/log.d/2026-08-30-owner-rulings-oi68-oi69.md`):\n12\t(a1) no-daemon — a retained transcript a bounded process replays, not an actor;\n13\t(b1) `reset_on_same_artifact = false` default; (c2) keep-warm pings THROUGH the\n14\tblackout (Anthropic only) — the plan's own §2/§3.5 \"skipped inside the blackout\"\n15\ttext is superseded by this ruling and the code follows the ruling; (d1) dial in\n16\t`docs/process.toml [adjudicator]`; (e1) dedicated CLI homes once the dial is on.\n17\t\n18\tDeviations from spec: keep-warm pings through the blackout per OI-69 (c2),\n19\tagainst the plan §2/§3.5 wording (Sol #17); recorded above and in the spec\n20\tContext.\n21\t\n22\t### REVIEW-A rework (round 002, CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=6)\n23\t\n24\tSession 003 died mid-rework on a provider usage limit; this session reconciled\n25\tits uncommitted residue (the fix shape was already in the tree), completed and\n26\tverified it. What the rework changes, finding by finding:\n27\t\n28\t1. MAJOR (store keyed by family only) — the store is now keyed by\n29\t   `(family, route_id)`: the route id is hashed into the filename and checked\n30\t   verbatim after parsing, so neither a misplaced file nor a stale family-only\n31\t   record crosses a route boundary; `load_family` enumerates one family's valid\n32\t   records for the dispatcher's keep-warm; `adjudicator_launch` refuses a\n33\t   missing route id. Driven: a stored `OPENAI-A` session is never resumed for\n34\t   `OPENAI-B` (`test_launch_never_resumes_another_route_of_the_same_family`).\n35\t2. MAJOR (governing hash omitted the judging templates) — `map_preflight` now\n36\t   returns the actual file each loaded prompt came from (override-aware);\n37\t   `resolve_session_setup` carries the four `adjudicate-*` paths on\n38\t   `LoopContext.adjudicator_prompt_paths`; `route_session` passes them to\n39\t   `adjudicator_launch`, whose `governing_hash` folds them in; a changed\n40\t   judging instruction drains the session and retires it at the next clear\n41\t   point. Driven at both ends:\n42\t   `test_governing_hash_changes_with_the_loaded_adjudication_template`,\n43\t   `test_preflight_surfaces_the_loaded_adjudication_template_to_the_hash`,\n44\t   `test_loaded_adjudication_prompt_change_retires_at_clear_point`.\n45\t3. MAJOR (OPENAI/OPENCODE never read their telemetry) —\n46\t   `adjudicator_session.context_telemetry` selects the reader by family:\n47\t   OPENAI joins the emitted `thread.started.thread_id` to the exact\n48\t   `rollout-*-<id>.jsonl` under the launch environment's `CODEX_HOME` (no\n49\t   `--last`, no ambient home — either could select another route's\n50\t   transcript); OPENCODE reads its own `--format json` stream.\n51\t   `adjudicator_bookkeeping` persists the captured id, so a later launch\n52\t   resumes instead of minting; `session_meta` merges the retained columns\n53\t   blank-by-blank over WI-535's one-shot tuple. Driven:\n54\t   `test_openai_bookkeeping_captures_thread_and_rollout_then_resumes`,\n55\t   `test_opencode_bookkeeping_captures_stream_session_then_resumes`.\n56\t4. MINOR (IF-174 Rationale cited history) — the cell now states only the\n57\t   standing reason; provenance lives here.\n58\t5. MINOR (IF-174 Data over ceiling, named a runtime path) — the cell is now a\n59\t   typed pointer to the owner contract (\"AdjudicatorSession record schema and\n60\t   callable API declared by Contract IF-174 in scripts/adjudicator_session\",\n61\t   108 chars vs the 160 ceiling).\n62\t6. MINOR (no contract on the owner) — `adjudicator_session.py`'s header now\n63\t   carries `Contracts: IF-174` and the `Contract IF-174:` body (record schema,\n64\t   compound identity, atomic writes, per-family readers, lifecycle purity).\n65\t\n66\tAdjacent consequences of the compound key: the dispatch keep-warm tick\n67\tenumerates `load_family(\"ANTHROPIC\")` instead of reading one family file;\n68\tLLR-163/TC-157 re-pointed at the adapter seam (`resume_template` joins\n69\t`split_cmd`/`build_argv`; TC-157 verifies IF-174's surface);\n70\t`IF-064`'s row names `scripts/adjudicator_session` a requestor of `split_cmd`.\n71\tRatchets re-stamped DELIBERATELY: module-size DOWN (agent_loop 2640 -> 2622,\n72\tagent_common 1300 -> 1299 — the bookkeeping body moved into\n73\t`adjudicator_session.bookkeep`, one home); the complexity baseline's\n74\t`route_session` entry dropped (the launch call now sits under the census\n75\tfloor). Smoke-budget membership: 1478 collected vs the 1482 ceiling — inside\n76\tthe stamped headroom, no re-stamp owed.\n77\t# fig: cmd=\"python -m pytest -q -n auto -m smoke --collect-only\" rev=6210a254-dirty\n78\t\n79\tPosture notes: the LLR-163/TC-157 amendments touch Approved cells without\n80\tre-statusing, so they ride as SNAPSHOT DRIFT to the next sitting (the\n81\tcheck_trajectory warning's own declared option — re-attestation is a human\n82\tact); docs/ratify/ and docs/open-items.html are trunk-owned generated families\n83\t(docs/stack.ini [generated]), so neither is regenerated on this branch.\n84\t\n85\tDeferred open items: none.\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efca4c5b-93ff-447e-9489-9229d57d664c","uuid":"47388cfd-f8d3-4e1c-a6e7-f4c0af99b5fe","timestamp":"2026-08-31T07:41:19.171Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-drive\\wi-540-adjudicator-retention-layer\\docs\\log.d\\WI-540-adjudicator-retention-layer.md","content":"## 2026-08-31 — WI-540: the adjudicator session-retention layer, shipped inert at dial 0\n\nPlan §5 step 3 of the adjudicator session-retention plan\n(`docs/plans/2026-08-29-adjudicator-session-retention-plan.md`). The layer that\nturns WI-535's telemetry into an opt-in retained session: a session store, a\nper-family resume-argv adapter, occupancy readers, the drain/reset rule and the\nkeep-warm tick — all guarded behind `[adjudicator] context_reset_pct`, shipped\nat `0` (inert: today's one-shot behaviour byte-for-byte). Turning the dial on\nand verifying it on-box is WI-541 (plan §5 step 4).\n\nOwner rulings honoured (OI-69, `docs/log.d/2026-08-30-owner-rulings-oi68-oi69.md`):\n(a1) no-daemon — a retained transcript a bounded process replays, not an actor;\n(b1) `reset_on_same_artifact = false` default; (c2) keep-warm pings THROUGH the\nblackout (Anthropic only) — the plan's own §2/§3.5 \"skipped inside the blackout\"\ntext is superseded by this ruling and the code follows the ruling; (d1) dial in\n`docs/process.toml [adjudicator]`; (e1) dedicated CLI homes once the dial is on.\n\nDeviations from spec: keep-warm pings through the blackout per OI-69 (c2),\nagainst the plan §2/§3.5 wording (Sol #17); recorded above and in the spec\nContext.\n\n### REVIEW-A rework (round 002, CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=6)\n\nSession 003 died mid-rework on a provider usage limit; this session reconciled\nits uncommitted residue (the fix shape was already in the tree), completed and\nverified it. What the rework changes, finding by finding:\n\n1. MAJOR (store keyed by family only) — the store is now keyed by\n   `(family, route_id)`: the route id is hashed into the filename and checked\n   verbatim after parsing, so neither a misplaced file nor a stale family-only\n   record crosses a route boundary; `load_family` enumerates one family's valid\n   records for the dispatcher's keep-warm; `adjudicator_launch` refuses a\n   missing route id. Driven: a stored `OPENAI-A` session is never resumed for\n   `OPENAI-B` (`test_launch_never_resumes_another_route_of_the_same_family`).\n2. MAJOR (governing hash omitted the judging templates) — `map_preflight` now\n   returns the actual file each loaded prompt came from (override-aware);\n   `resolve_session_setup` carries the four `adjudicate-*` paths on\n   `LoopContext.adjudicator_prompt_paths`; `route_session` passes them to\n   `adjudicator_launch`, whose `governing_hash` folds them in; a changed\n   judging instruction drains the session and retires it at the next clear\n   point. Driven at both ends:\n   `test_governing_hash_changes_with_the_loaded_adjudication_template`,\n   `test_preflight_surfaces_the_loaded_adjudication_template_to_the_hash`,\n   `test_loaded_adjudication_prompt_change_retires_at_clear_point`.\n3. MAJOR (OPENAI/OPENCODE never read their telemetry) —\n   `adjudicator_session.context_telemetry` selects the reader by family:\n   OPENAI joins the emitted `thread.started.thread_id` to the exact\n   `rollout-*-<id>.jsonl` under the launch environment's `CODEX_HOME` (no\n   `--last`, no ambient home — either could select another route's\n   transcript); OPENCODE reads its own `--format json` stream.\n   `adjudicator_bookkeeping` persists the captured id, so a later launch\n   resumes instead of minting; `session_meta` merges the retained columns\n   blank-by-blank over WI-535's one-shot tuple. Driven:\n   `test_openai_bookkeeping_captures_thread_and_rollout_then_resumes`,\n   `test_opencode_bookkeeping_captures_stream_session_then_resumes`.\n4. MINOR (IF-174 Rationale cited history) — the cell now states only the\n   standing reason; provenance lives here.\n5. MINOR (IF-174 Data over ceiling, named a runtime path) — the cell is now a\n   typed pointer to the owner contract (\"AdjudicatorSession record schema and\n   callable API declared by Contract IF-174 in scripts/adjudicator_session\",\n   108 chars vs the 160 ceiling).\n6. MINOR (no contract on the owner) — `adjudicator_session.py`'s header now\n   carries `Contracts: IF-174` and the `Contract IF-174:` body (record schema,\n   compound identity, atomic writes, per-family readers, lifecycle purity).\n\nAdjacent consequences of the compound key: the dispatch keep-warm tick\nenumerates `load_family(\"ANTHROPIC\")` instead of reading one family file;\nLLR-163/TC-157 re-pointed at the adapter seam (`resume_template` joins\n`split_cmd`/`build_argv`; TC-157 verifies IF-174's surface);\n`IF-064`'s row names `scripts/adjudicator_session` a requestor of `split_cmd`.\nRatchets re-stamped DELIBERATELY: module-size DOWN (agent_loop 2640 -> 2622,\nagent_common 1300 -> 1299 — the bookkeeping body moved into\n`adjudicator_session.bookkeep`, one home); the complexity baseline's\n`route_session` entry dropped (the launch call now sits under the census\nfloor). Smoke-budget membership: 1478 collected vs the 1482 ceiling — inside\nthe stamped headroom, no re-stamp owed.\n# fig: cmd=\"python -m pytest -q -n auto -m smoke --collect-only\" rev=6210a254-dirty\n\nPosture notes: the LLR-163/TC-157 amendments touch Approved cells without\nre-statusing, so they ride as SNAPSHOT DRIFT to the next sitting (the\ncheck_trajectory warning's own declared option — re-attestation is a human\nact); docs/ratify/ and docs/open-items.html are trunk-owned generated families\n(docs/stack.ini [generated]), so neither is regenerated on this branch.\n\nDeferred open items: none.\n","numLines":86,"startLine":1,"totalLines":86}}}
