{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UtauBfMnwYLP81fmWKmCMb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t<!-- Copied verbatim on 2026-08-30 from C:/Projects/ai-template-plans/adjudicator-persistent-session/PLAN-OPTIN-LAYER.md — the plan of record for the rows that cite it; its companions there (the source reports, the prototype, the drafts, the review transcripts) stay outside the repo. -->\n2\t\n3\t# Adjudicator session retention — the opt-in layer\n4\t\n5\tDate: 2026-08-29. Owner decision (this date): design it as an **opt-in layer** with a single\n6\tdial, `0` = today's behaviour byte-for-byte. Motivation recorded from the owner: in a prior run\n7\tthe adjudicator was spun up for every small work item, relearned and reloaded the spine and the\n8\tsurrounding items each time, and usage was extreme; when a session *was* kept, its context\n9\tfilled quickly (it needs the full spine plus neighbouring items) and the choice was compaction\n10\t(poor quality) or a full reload (the same tokens again). The layer must protect against both:\n11\t**retain context that would otherwise be reloaded, and reset the session ourselves before the\n12\tprovider compacts.** Online guidance places session degradation past ~60%; the dial lets the\n13\towner sit below that.\n14\t\n15\tSupersedes the sequencing in `PLAN.md` §5 (the A/B gate is dropped by owner decision; the\n16\tmechanics, matrix and Sol-review corrections in `PLAN.md` still apply and are referenced).\n17\t\n18\t---\n19\t\n20\t## 1. Shape in one paragraph\n21\t\n22\tEvery adjudication is still **one bounded headless process** exactly as today — same\n23\t`run_session`, same closed stdin, same 7200 s timeout, same tree kill, same per-session\n24\ttelemetry. The only difference when the dial is on: the process is launched with the family's\n25\t*resume* form (`claude -p --resume <id>` / `codex exec resume <id>` / `opencode run --session\n26\t<id>`) against a session the orchestrator minted earlier, so the model arrives already holding\n27\tthe spine and the prior work items. After each adjudication the orchestrator reads that\n28\tfamily's occupancy from the process's own telemetry; when `occupancy ≥ dial` the session is\n29\tmarked draining and is retired at the next **clear point** (idle, waiting o
